findings.description:
Inside the RuntimeException catch: "if (e instanceof jakarta.ws.rs.NotFoundException) {
      log.debug("Repository config file not found: {}", path);
      return Fetched.ABSENT;
    }". This PR removed every REST client from this path — getInstallationClient/getRepository/hub4j's getFileContent replaced the JAX-RS clients — and the catch two blocks down documents the actual 404 signal: "// hub4j signals a missing file with FileNotFoundException (an IOException)." with "catch (java.io.FileNotFoundException e)" returning ABSENT. Nothing remaining on this path (the Quarkiverse client provider and its hub4j calls, and snakeyaml parsing) produces a jakarta.ws.rs.NotFoundException, so the instanceof can never be true. It is unreachable leftover from the client migration; a reader trusting it would believe JAX-RS 404s still arrive here. Removing the branch is behavior-neutral; it misleads rather than misbehaves, but a maintainer migrating the next resolver should not copy it.
